Description: dashenc: default CMAF-strict movflags on inner mp4 muxer
 Plex Web's Chromium MSE rejects DASH segments that re-embed a moov
 box per chunk. Stock dashenc's `+dash` movflag does flip
 `FF_MOV_FLAG_EMPTY_MOOV` + `FF_MOV_FLAG_DEFAULT_BASE_MOOF` in movenc,
 so on paper the per-segment moov should already be empty. In
 practice scaleplex still needed `+separate_moof` (audio/video in
 distinct moof atoms — MSE source buffers track them independently)
 and `+cmaf` (CMAF profile compliance, which adds
 `FF_MOV_FLAG_NEGATIVE_CTS_OFFSETS` so b-frame CTS offsets stay valid
 across fragments). Live regression observed sha-019a335 (2026-05):
 without these, Plex Web playback oscillated between "playing" and
 "buffering" past the first ~1s of content.
 .
 Worker rewriter used to inject these via
 `-format_options movflags=+empty_moov+default_base_moof+separate_moof+cmaf`
 spliced before `-f dash`. With this patch the dashenc init applies
 them directly to the inner mp4 muxer options dict — the rewriter
 inject becomes redundant and can be retired.
 .
 Notable: NO `+frag_keyframe`. With h264_vaapi's default GOP shorter
 than our 3s segment, frag_keyframe forced a new moof at every
 keyframe, producing chunks with two moof+mdat pairs which Plex
 Web's MSE could buffer but couldn't seek into cleanly. dashenc
 already sets `+frag_custom` so the segment muxer drives fragmentation
 (one moof per segment file) — we don't add it here.
Origin: scaleplex
Forwarded: not-needed
Author: scaleplex
Last-Update: 2026-05-12
---
--- a/libavformat/dashenc.c
+++ b/libavformat/dashenc.c
@@ -1649,6 +1649,16 @@ static int dash_init(AVFormatContext *s)
             // the player resyncs its timebase on seek-resume sessions.
             if (c->skip_to_segment > 1)
                 av_dict_set(&opts, "movflags", "+frag_discont", AV_DICT_APPEND);
+
+            // scaleplex: CMAF-strict movflags so Plex Web's Chromium MSE
+            // accepts the segments. +cmaf preset (movenc.c) implies
+            // +empty_moov + +default_base_moof + negative_cts_offsets;
+            // +separate_moof keeps audio + video in distinct moof
+            // atoms which MSE buffers separately. Was previously
+            // injected via worker rewriter -format_options; now native.
+            av_dict_set(&opts, "movflags",
+                        "+empty_moov+default_base_moof+separate_moof+cmaf",
+                        AV_DICT_APPEND);
             if (os->frag_type == FRAG_TYPE_EVERY_FRAME)
                 av_dict_set(&opts, "movflags", "+frag_every_frame", AV_DICT_APPEND);
             else
